{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","statement":"AIDR (Artificial Intelligence for Disaster Response) is an online platform that lets any person or organization collect tweets related to a disaster event.","source_span":"Artificial Intelligence for Disaster Response (AIDR) is an online platform to support this cause"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","statement":"The total volume of all tweets can be huge, about 350 thousand tweets per minute.","source_span":"about 350 thousand tweets per minute"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","statement":"Tweets are only 140 characters long, making them hard to understand without enough context.","source_span":"tweets are short – only 140 characters"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","statement":"For the event-only binary classification task, the CNN model outperformed in four out of five tasks with an accuracy gain of up to 4.5 absolute points.","source_span":"the CNN model outperformed in four out of five tasks with an accuracy gain of up to 4.5 absolute points"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","statement":"In the scenario of no event data, the CNN model shows a substantial improvement of up to 18 absolute points over several non-neural models.","source_span":"the CNN model shows substantial improvement of up to 18 absolute points over the several non-neural models"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","statement":"The authors propose an extension that combines a multilayer perceptron with a CNN (MLP-CNN).","source_span":"we propose an extension that combines multilayer perceptron with a CNN"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","statement":"The authors apply a simple event selection technique based on TF-IDF to select out-of-event data most similar to the event under consideration.","source_span":"we apply a simple event selection technique based on TF-IDF and select only those events that are most similar to the event under consideration"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What is AIDR and what does it allow users to do during a disaster?","answer":"AIDR (Artificial Intelligence for Disaster Response) is an online platform that any person or organization can use during a disaster to collect tweets related to the event."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","fact_refs":[1],"question":"According to the paper, approximately how many tweets are posted per minute in total?","answer":"About 350 thousand tweets per minute."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","fact_refs":[2],"question":"How many characters long are tweets, according to the paper's discussion of classification difficulty?","answer":"Tweets are only 140 characters long, which makes them hard to understand without sufficient context."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","fact_refs":[3],"question":"How much did the CNN model improve accuracy over state-of-the-art methods on the event-only binary classification task?","answer":"The CNN model outperformed state-of-the-art methods in four out of five tasks, with an accuracy gain of up to 4.5 absolute points."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","fact_refs":[4],"question":"How much better did the CNN model perform compared to non-neural models when no event-specific labeled data was available?","answer":"The CNN model showed a substantial improvement of up to 18 absolute points over several non-neural models in the no-event-data scenario."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0067","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What technique did the authors use to select useful out-of-event data for training?","answer":"They applied a simple event selection technique based on TF-IDF, selecting only the events most similar to the event under consideration."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","statement":"The encoder-decoder models were trained on a single NVIDIA Tesla K40 GPU with mini-batches of 32 sentences, a learning rate of 0.01, dropout rate of 0.1, and the AdaGrad optimizer.","source_span":"we trained the encoder-decoder models on a single GPU (NVIDIA Tesla K40), with mini-batches of 32 sentences, learning rate of 0.01, dropout rate of 0.1, and the AdaGrad optimizer"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","statement":"Training the encoder-decoder takes approximately 10 days and is stopped after 5 epochs with no loss improvement on a validation set.","source_span":"training takes approximately 10 days and is stopped after 5 epochs with no loss improvement on a validation set"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","statement":"The best tuned classifier for the prediction tasks is a feed-forward network with one hidden layer and ReLU activation, hidden layer size equal to input size, dropout rate 0.8, learning rate 0.01, optimized with AdaGrad.","source_span":"Our best tuned classifier, which we use for all experiments, is a feed-forward network with one hidden layer and a ReLU activation function...We use a dropout rate of 0.8 and a learning rate of 0.01."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","statement":"Significance tests were conducted using the paired t-test, and all results reported in the summary of findings are highly significant with p-value < 0.0001.","source_span":"we use the paired t-test...All the results reported in the summery of findings are highly significant (p-value INLINEFORM0 0.0001)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","statement":"The comparison between the encoder-decoder (ED) with size 500 and ED with size 750 on the word order task was not significant, with a p-value of 0.11.","source_span":"ED with size 500 and ED with size 750 tested on the word order task (p-value=0.11)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","statement":"The comparison between CBOW with dimensions 750 and CBOW with dimensions 1000 was not significant, with a p-value of 0.3.","source_span":"CBOW with dimensions 750 and 1000 (p-value=0.3)"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","fact_refs":[0],"question":"What hardware and hyperparameters were used to train the encoder-decoder sentence embedding models?","answer":"A single NVIDIA Tesla K40 GPU was used, with mini-batches of 32 sentences, a learning rate of 0.01, dropout rate of 0.1, and the AdaGrad optimizer."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","fact_refs":[1],"question":"How long did training the encoder-decoder model take and under what condition was training stopped?","answer":"Training took approximately 10 days and was stopped after 5 epochs with no loss improvement on the validation set."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What is the architecture of the best-tuned classifier used for the auxiliary prediction tasks?","answer":"It is a feed-forward network with one hidden layer (size equal to the input vector) using ReLU activation, a dropout rate of 0.8, a learning rate of 0.01, and the AdaGrad optimizer."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What statistical test did the authors use to assess significance, and what significance level did most results reach?","answer":"They used the paired t-test, and most reported results were highly significant with a p-value less than 0.0001."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What was the p-value for the comparison between encoder-decoder models of size 500 and size 750 on the word order task?","answer":"The p-value was 0.11, meaning the difference was not significant."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0068","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What was the p-value for the comparison between CBOW models with 750 and 1000 dimensions?","answer":"The p-value was 0.3, indicating no significant difference."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","statement":"The study analyzes cohesion and coalitions in the Eighth European Parliament, covering the term 2014-2019.","source_span":"the Eighth European Parliament (2014--2019)"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","statement":"The analysis uses two diverse datasets: a roll-call vote dataset and a Twitter retweet dataset.","source_span":"We make use of two diverse datasets in the analysis."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","statement":"Two methodologies are employed: one based on Krippendorff's Alpha reliability and one based on Exponential Random Graph Models (ERGM).","source_span":"The first one is based on Krippendorff's Alpha reliability, used to measure the agreement between raters in data-analysis scenarios, and the second one is based on Exponential Random Graph Models"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","statement":"Twitter has over 300 million monthly active users and 500 million tweets posted daily.","source_span":"With over 300 million monthly active users and 500 million tweets posted daily"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","statement":"A roll-call vote (RCV) is a parliamentary vote in which the names of the MEPs are recorded along with their votes, available as part of the minutes of the parliament's plenary sessions.","source_span":"A roll-call vote (RCV) is a vote in the parliament in which the names of the MEPs are recorded along with their votes."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","statement":"The differences between the Krippendorff's Alpha and ERGM results are due to the different treatment of non-attending and abstaining MEPs by the two methodologies.","source_span":"the difference are due to the different treatment of non-attending and abstaining MEPs by INLINEFORM0 and ERGM"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","fact_refs":[0],"question":"Which term of the European Parliament does this study on cohesion and coalitions cover?","answer":"The Eighth European Parliament, covering the term 2014-2019."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","fact_refs":[1],"question":"What two datasets does the study use to analyze MEP behavior?","answer":"A roll-call vote dataset and a Twitter (retweet) dataset."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","fact_refs":[2],"question":"What two methodologies are used to analyze cohesion and coalitions among political groups?","answer":"Krippendorff's Alpha reliability, used to measure agreement between raters, and Exponential Random Graph Models (ERGM), a network-based approach."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","fact_refs":[3],"question":"How many monthly active users and daily tweets does Twitter have, according to the paper?","answer":"Over 300 million monthly active users and 500 million tweets posted daily."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","fact_refs":[4],"question":"What is a roll-call vote (RCV) as defined in the paper?","answer":"It is a parliamentary vote in which the names of the MEPs are recorded along with their votes, available as part of the minutes of the parliament's plenary sessions."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d2_doc0069","fact_refs":[5],"question":"Why do the Krippendorff's Alpha and ERGM methodologies produce somewhat different results in this study?","answer":"The differences are due to the two methodologies' different treatment of non-attending and abstaining MEPs."}
